                        e.g.: ${PROGNAME} -i -arch
                              ${PROGNAME} -i my_env -arch

    -i -arch-push       Install with intel scope (shared install_tree) then push built packages to ARCH buildcache.
                              ${PROGNAME} -i -arch-push

── admin 3-stage collaborative workflow ──────────────────────────────────────

    Stage 1 — any admin: build in personal scratch space
    Stage 2 — admin with GPG key: push signed package to shared cache
    Stage 3 — admin with GPG key: deploy from cache to shared install_tree

    --cache-push <pkg>@<ver>
                        Push a specific package (built with intel scope) to ARCH cache.
                        Requires admin group + GPG key. Shows preview before pushing.
                        e.g.: ${PROGNAME} --cache-push python@3.11.9
                              ${PROGNAME} --cache-push --env locally   (push full env)

    --deploy <pkg>@<ver>
                        Deploy a signed package from ARCH cache → ${SPACK_INSTALL_TREE}
                        Requires admin group + trusted GPG key. Uses --use-buildcache only.
                        e.g.: ${PROGNAME} --deploy python@3.11.9
                              ${PROGNAME} --deploy --env locally        (deploy full env)

    -r | --remove       Remove Spack inside user directory

    -m | --merge        Merge multiple YAML files into a single YAML file.
                        Files are merged in order, such that files listed later will override files listed earlier.
                        e.g.: ${PROGNAME} -m file1.yaml file2.yaml ...

    -e | --env          Move the enviromenst to another path
                        e.g:  ${PROGNAME} -e /data/$(id -gn)/spack_enviroments/$(id -un)

    -u | --update [dev] Upgrade Spack (default: latest stable release tag)
                        --update dev  clones the latest develop branch instead
                        NOTE: Backs up current spack as spack.MonDD.YYYY, preserves arch config and environments

More help:
EOF

1>&2 cat << \EOF

── Custom config scopes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  intel  → install_tree: ${SPACK_INSTALL_TREE}        (intel)
  amd         → install_tree: ${SPACK_INSTALL_TREE_AMD}   (amd)

  Use -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel or -C /apps/helpers/spack/amd to switch targets.

── Installing packages on ARCH manually ────────────────────────────────────

  spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ config get config   ( verify install_tree )
  spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ find -pl
  spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ concretize -f
  spack -ddd -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ install -j 8

  amd:
  spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/amd/ concretize -f
  spack -ddd -C /apps/helpers/spack/amd/ install -j 8

── Mirrors and build cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Mirror config (single source of truth):
    /apps/helpers/spack/intel/mirrors.yaml    (intel)
    /apps/helpers/spack/amd/mirrors.yaml  (amd)

  To change a mirror path, edit mirrors.yaml — all users pick it up automatically.

  List active mirrors:
    spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ mirror list

  Search buildcache for a package:
    spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ buildcache list python

  Install from buildcache (prefer cached binary, build if missing):
    spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ install --use-buildcache prefer python@3.11

  Install from buildcache only (fail if not cached):
    spack -C /apps/helpers/spack/intel/ install --use-buildcache only python@3.11

  Push a built package to the local ARCH mirror:
    spackon --cache-push python@3.11    # safe: intel scope check + dry-run confirm

  Trust buildcache signing keys:
    spackon --keys trust

── 3-stage collaborative workflow (${SPACK_SCRATCH}) ────────────────────

  Shared scratch space: ${SPACK_SCRATCH}  (all admin members build here)

  Stage 1 — any admin (build + test in personal space):
    export SPACK_ROOT=${SPACK_SCRATCH}
    spackon -i locally             # build packages, test locally

  Stage 2 — admin with GPG key (contribute to shared cache):
    spackon --cache-push python@3.11.9
    # only pushes packages built with intel scope
    # shows preview + requires confirmation before pushing

  Stage 3 — admin with trusted key (deploy to shared install_tree):
    spackon --deploy python@3.11.9
    # installs --use-buildcache only → ${SPACK_INSTALL_TREE}
    # fails if package is unsigned or key not trusted

